<!-- Cover — the title layout in slot mode. The five slots (kicker, title, subtitle, author, date)
     become the theme's grid areas on the web and real p:ph placeholders in PPTX.
     Not a single line of alignment is written here — the theme owns where the slot areas sit. So
     swapping the theme puts the same source at the center (minimal), the bottom (editorial), the
     middle left (ink) or the top left (harbor).

     The title text is a gradient between two accents (`gradient(accent1 accent6, 90deg)`). The
     colors are token names, so when the theme changes both ends of the gradient follow its palette. -->
<slide id="cover" layout="title" enter="rise">
  <text slot="kicker" variant="kicker">Slide Oriented Markup Language</text>
  <h1 slot="title" size="96"><span color="gradient(accent1 accent6, 90deg)">balpyo</span></h1>
  <text slot="subtitle" role="heading" color="muted">Write your slides once —
  get the web and an editable PPTX</text>
  <text slot="author" role="body">Render engine · Themes · CLI</text>
  <text slot="date" role="caption">This deck is twelve SOML slides, rendered by balpyo</text>
  <note>The deck is itself the output — what you are looking at and the PPTX we shipped come from the same source.</note>
</slide>
